WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.716 --> 00:00:02.466
(super high speed speaking)

00:00:02.466 --> 00:00:05.273
(jazzy music)

00:00:05.273 --> 00:00:06.857
- I think it's going to be interesting

00:00:06.857 --> 00:00:08.203
because I talk a lot.

00:00:08.203 --> 00:00:10.001
I can't shut up.

00:00:10.001 --> 00:00:12.010
- I've always been very
intrigued by the idea of silence

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:13.954
as someone that does a lot of of talking.

00:00:13.954 --> 00:00:15.569
- I think people are
going to be uncomfortable.

00:00:15.569 --> 00:00:17.209
I think that's going to
make me uncomfortable,

00:00:17.209 --> 00:00:19.609
and then I'm not going
to know how to respond.

00:00:19.609 --> 00:00:22.433
- Even when I have strep throat
I still find ways to talk.

00:00:22.433 --> 00:00:23.405
(whip)

00:00:23.405 --> 00:00:26.405
(three bells chime)

00:00:28.073 --> 00:00:29.362
(whip)

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.070
(old fashioned jazz)

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:35.028
- [Voiceover] Do we need any new towels?

00:00:35.028 --> 00:00:36.491
How many do we have right now?

00:00:36.491 --> 00:00:39.680
- I could not communicate
something easily whatsoever.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:40.888
Not even to save my life.

00:00:40.888 --> 00:00:41.721
- [Voiceover] You hungry?

00:00:41.721 --> 00:00:42.554
Alright.

00:00:42.554 --> 00:00:44.137
Tacos?

00:00:44.137 --> 00:00:46.395
You like Thai food?

00:00:46.395 --> 00:00:48.450
- I could tell by the fourth,
when he finally got it right,

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.533
he's very exacerbated with me.

00:00:49.533 --> 00:00:51.116
- [Voiceover] Eggs?

00:00:52.741 --> 00:00:53.741
Over medium?

00:00:55.074 --> 00:00:56.907
Veggie bacon?

00:00:56.907 --> 00:00:58.654
Turkey bacon?

00:00:58.654 --> 00:01:02.362
- As the meal went on, the
waiter stopped talking.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:05.195
- [Voiceover] You're going
to share the fiesta nachos?

00:01:05.195 --> 00:01:07.903
Would you like any meat in it?

00:01:07.903 --> 00:01:08.736
Chicken?

00:01:11.986 --> 00:01:13.444
- [Voiceover] No, I don't
think that was like too harsh.

00:01:13.444 --> 00:01:15.277
Is that what you mean?

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.540
I don't think it was overbearing.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:21.780
- I feel like very
gesture now is cataloged.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.863
Like I have a dictionary of gestures.

00:01:29.738 --> 00:01:32.307
Walk across the street to
get something to drink?

00:01:32.307 --> 00:01:33.307
(whip)

00:01:33.307 --> 00:01:34.148
(funky rock music)

00:01:34.148 --> 00:01:36.601
- It was a lot harder than I
thought to not speak at all.

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:37.641
I think I think a lot more now

00:01:37.641 --> 00:01:39.794
about how I use words and when.

00:01:39.794 --> 00:01:41.203
- I am so relieved.

00:01:41.203 --> 00:01:43.289
I felt there were so many
things that I left unsaid

00:01:43.289 --> 00:01:45.394
because I had no way of communicating it.

00:01:45.394 --> 00:01:47.538
- I think this did show me what it's like

00:01:47.538 --> 00:01:49.202
to really listen to people more.

00:01:49.202 --> 00:01:50.866
- I think I'm definitely more attuned now

00:01:50.866 --> 00:01:53.513
to other people's nonverbal cues.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:54.602
- The biggest think that I learned

00:01:54.602 --> 00:01:57.537
is how lonely you can feel
surrounded by so many people

00:01:57.537 --> 00:01:59.538
but you still feel like
you're in this place

00:01:59.538 --> 00:02:00.825
where nobody can reach you.

00:02:00.825 --> 00:02:02.913
- I think what this
taught me about listening

00:02:02.913 --> 00:02:04.985
was how to really hone in

00:02:04.985 --> 00:02:09.346
on what the person I was
speaking to really means.

00:02:09.346 --> 00:02:10.753
- I think overall I've learned

00:02:10.753 --> 00:02:13.601
that the ability to speak
when you want and how you want

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:15.994
is truly powerful and it's not something

00:02:15.994 --> 00:02:18.257
I would be giving up any time soon.

00:02:18.257 --> 00:02:20.757
(funky music)

00:02:24.545 --> 00:02:25.753
(squeaky door)

